#229 The checkpoint eviction system has two layers: (a) during `create_checkpoint()`, checkpoints within `checkpoint_min_step` tokens of a previous checkpoint are proactively erased (unless created by the current task, lines 2522–2527), and (b) the hard-cap LRU eviction at line 2535 erases the oldest checkpoint when `n_ctx_checkpoints` is reached. The working record's earlier entry correctly described only layer (b) — layer (a) was omitted.

