Now, to answer the original question about **checkpoint behavior** in beellama (since `n_before_user` doesn't exist in this fork):

### Checkpoint System in beellama

**What it is:** Context checkpoints are in-memory snapshots of the KV cache taken during prompt evaluation, enabling fast rollback when the prompt changes (e.g., user edits a message, speculative decoding needs to restart).

**Key struct** (`common/common.h:1214`):
```cpp
struct common_prompt_checkpoint {
    int64_t n_tokens;
    int id_task = -1;
    llama_pos pos_min;
    llama_pos pos_max;
    std::vector<uint8_t> data_tgt;  // target model KV snapshot
    std::vector<uint8_t> data_dft;  // draft model KV snapshot
    std::vector<uint8_t> data_spec; // speculative decoder internal state
    // ... update_tgt/load_tgt/update_dft/load_dft/clear methods
};
```

**Per-slot storage** (`server-task.h:614-617`):
```cpp
struct server_prompt {
    server_tokens tokens;
    std::list<common_prompt_checkpoint> checkpoints;
    // ...
};
```

**When checkpoints are created** (`server-context.cpp:3832-3912`):
```cpp
// break at the last user message, or at user messages at least min step past the last checkpoint
if (do_checkpoint && spans.is_user_start(slot.prompt.n_tokens())) {
    const auto pos = slot.prompt.n_tokens();
    const auto & checkpoints = slot.prompt.checkpoints;
    if (pos == last_user_pos || checkpoints.empty() || pos > checkpoints.back().n_tokens + params_base.checkpoint_min_step) {
        break;
    }
}
// ... later:
// skip ordinary mid-prompt checkpoints, unless the batch starts a user
// message or we are near the end of the prompt
if (!is_user_start && !near_prompt_end) {
    do_checkpoint = false;
}
```

Checkpoints are created at two strategic points:
1. **At user message boundaries** — when `spans.is_user_start()` is true and the position is at least `checkpoint_min_step` (default 8192 tokens) past the last checkpoint
2. **Near the end of the prompt** — within `n_ubatch + 4` tokens of the prompt end, so the final batch can be re-evaluated independently

**Configuration** (`common/common.h:736-737`):
```cpp
int32_t n_ctx_checkpoints   = 32;    // max number of context checkpoints per slot
int32_t checkpoint_min_step = 8192;  // minimum spacing between context checkpoints
```

**Checkpoint restoration** during speculative rollback (`server-context.cpp:3585-3620`):
