## How Prompt Cache and Slot Reuse Work

### Overview

The server uses a two-tier slot reuse strategy:

1. **Hot slot reuse** — reusing a slot whose current prompt shares a long common prefix with the new task's prompt (controlled by `slot_prompt_similarity` threshold)
2. **LRU fallback** — picking the least-recently-used idle slot when no similar prompt is found

Before reusing a slot, the existing prompt's KV cache state is **saved** to a secondary prompt cache (`server_prompt_cache`), then the slot attempts to **load** a better-matching prompt from that cache. If loading succeeds, the slot's KV context is restored from cache and only the new tokens need to be decoded.

---

### Tier 1: `get_available_slot()` — Slot Selection by LCP Similarity

In `server-context.cpp` (line 1586), `get_available_slot()` first checks if `slot_prompt_similarity` is configured (non-zero). If so, it scans all idle slots and computes the similarity as the **Longest Common Prefix (LCP)** length divided by the new task's token count:

```cpp
// find the slot that has at least n% prompt similarity
if (slot_prompt_similarity != 0.0f) {
    float sim_best = 0;

    for (server_slot & slot : slots) {
        // ... skip processing slots and empty slots ...

        const auto & tokens = slot.prompt.tokens;

        // fraction of the Longest Common Prefix length with respect to the input prompt length
        const float sim_cur = float(tokens.get_common_prefix(task.tokens)) / task.tokens.size();

        // select the current slot if the criteria match
        if (sim_cur > sim_best && sim_cur > slot_prompt_similarity) {
            sim_best = sim_cur;
            ret = &slot;
        }
    }

    if (ret != nullptr) {
        const float f_keep = (sim_best*task.tokens.size()) / ret->prompt.tokens.size();

        // if we are about to lose a large portion of the existing context - save it in the prompt cache
        if (f_keep < 0.5f) {
            update_cache = true;
        }
    }
}
```

If no slot meets the similarity threshold, it falls back to LRU:

```cpp
// find the slot that has been least recently used
if (ret == nullptr) {
    int64_t t_last = -1;

    for (server_slot & slot : slots) {
        if (slot.is_processing()) {
            continue;
        }

        if (!ret || slot.t_last_used <= t_last) {
            t_last = slot.t_last_used;
            ret = &slot;
        }
    }

    if (ret != nullptr) {
        update_cache = true;
    }
}
```

### Cache Save → Load Cycle

Once a slot is selected, if `update_cache` is true, the slot's current prompt is saved to the prompt cache, then the slot tries to load a better match:

```cpp
if (update_cache) {
    ret->prompt_save(*prompt_cache);   // save current slot state to cache

    if (!ret->prompt_load(*prompt_cache, task.tokens)) {
        ret->prompt_clear(false);      // fallback: clear if no cache hit
    }

    prompt_cache->update();            // evict old entries if over limits
}
```

### Tier 2: `server_prompt_cache::load()` — Common-Prefix Matching in the Cache

In `server-task.cpp` (line 1678), `load()` finds the best cached prompt by iterating all cached states and computing LCP against the new tokens:

```cpp
bool server_prompt_cache::load(server_prompt & prompt, const server_tokens & tokens_new,
                                llama_context * ctx_tgt, llama_context * ctx_dft, int32_t id_slot) {
    const int lcp_best = prompt.tokens.get_common_prefix(tokens_new);

    float f_keep_best = prompt.tokens.size() > 0 ? float(lcp_best) / prompt.tokens.size() : -1.0f;
    float sim_best    = float(lcp_best) / tokens_new.size();

    auto it_best = states.end();

    // find the most similar cached prompt, that would also preserve the most context
    for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end(); ++it) {
        const int lcp_cur = it->tokens.get_common_prefix(tokens_new);

        const float f_keep_cur = float(lcp_cur) / it->tokens.size();
        const float sim_cur    = float(lcp_cur) / tokens_new.size();

        // don't trash large prompts
        if (f_keep_cur < 0.25f) {
            continue;
        }

        if (f_keep_best < f_keep_cur && sim_best < sim_cur) {
            f_keep_best = f_keep_cur;
            sim_best    = sim_cur;
            it_best = it;
        }
    }

    if (it_best != states.end()) {
        // ... restore KV state via llama_state_seq_set_data_ext ...
        prompt = std::move(*it_best);
        states.erase(it_best);
    }

    return true;
}
```

Key detail: a cached entry is only considered if `f_keep_cur >= 0.25` — i.e., at least 25% of the cached prompt's tokens would be preserved. This prevents trashing a large cached context for a marginal match.

### The Core Primitive: `get_common_prefix()`

In `server-common.cpp` (line 471), this is a simple token-by-token comparison (with special handling for multimodal `LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL` placeholders):

```cpp
size_t server_tokens::get_common_prefix(const server_tokens & b) const {
    const size_t max_idx = std::min(tokens.size(), b.tokens.size());

    if (!has_mtmd) {
        for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
            if (tokens[i] == b.tokens[i]) {
                continue;
            }
            return i;
        }
        return max_idx;
    }

    // multimodal path: LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL markers are compared by chunk ID and token count
    for (size_t i = 0; i < max_idx; ++i) {
        const llama_token ai = tokens[i];
        const llama_token bi = b.tokens[i];

        if (ai == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL && bi == LLAMA_TOKEN_NULL) {
            const auto & a_chunk = find_chunk(i);
            const auto & b_chunk = b.find_chunk(i);
            const std::string id_ai = mtmd_input_chunk_get_id(a_chunk.get());
            const std::string id_bi = mtmd_input_chunk_get_id(b_chunk.get());
            const size_t n_tok_a = mtmd_input_chunk_get_n_tokens(a_chunk.get());
            const size_t n_tok_b = mtmd_input_chunk_get_n_tokens(b_chunk.get());

            if (id_ai == id_bi && n_tok_a == n_tok_b) {
                i += n_tok_a - 1; // skip ahead past the media tokens
                continue;
            }
            return i;
        }

        if (ai == bi) {
            continue;
        }
        return i;
    }

    return max_idx; // all tokens are equal
