## Layer 2: Persistent Prompt Cache (`server_prompt_cache`)

### Saving (`alloc`)

When a slot's prompt is saved, `alloc()` checks if it's redundant or subsumes existing entries:

```cpp
// server-task.cpp:1623-1645
server_prompt * server_prompt_cache::alloc(const server_prompt & prompt, size_t state_size_tgt, size_t state_size_dft) {
    // first check if the current state is contained fully in the cache
    for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end(); ++it) {
        const int cur_lcp_len = it->tokens.get_common_prefix(prompt.tokens);
        if (cur_lcp_len == (int) prompt.tokens.size()) {
            SRV_TRC("%s", " - prompt is already in the cache, skipping\n");
            return nullptr;
        }
    }

    // next, remove any cached prompts that are fully contained in the current prompt
    for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end();) {
        const int len = it->tokens.get_common_prefix(prompt.tokens);
        if (len == (int) it->tokens.size()) {
            SRV_TRC(" - removing obsolete cached prompt with length %d\n", len);
            it = states.erase(it);
        } else {
            ++it;
        }
    }
    // ... allocates KV state buffers and pushes new entry
}
```

### Loading (`load`) — the common-prefix matching core

This is the heart of cache lookup. It iterates all cached prompts, computing two metrics per candidate:

- **`f_keep`** — fraction of the *cached* prompt that would be preserved (avoids trashing large cached prompts)
- **`sim`** — fraction of the *new* prompt that would be covered (maximizes reuse)

```cpp
// server-task.cpp:1678-1710
bool server_prompt_cache::load(server_prompt & prompt, const server_tokens & tokens_new,
                                llama_context * ctx_tgt, llama_context * ctx_dft, int32_t id_slot) {
    const int lcp_best = prompt.tokens.get_common_prefix(tokens_new);

    float f_keep_best = prompt.tokens.size() > 0 ? float(lcp_best) / prompt.tokens.size() : -1.0f;
    float sim_best    = float(lcp_best) / tokens_new.size();

    auto it_best = states.end();

    // find the most similar cached prompt, that would also preserve the most context
    for (auto it = states.begin(); it != states.end(); ++it) {
        const int lcp_cur = it->tokens.get_common_prefix(tokens_new);

        const float f_keep_cur = float(lcp_cur) / it->tokens.size();
        const float sim_cur    = float(lcp_cur) / tokens_new.size();

        // don't trash large prompts
        if (f_keep_cur < 0.25f) {
            continue;
        }

        if (f_keep_best < f_keep_cur && sim_best < sim_cur) {
            f_keep_best = f_keep_cur;
            sim_best    = sim_cur;
            it_best = it;
        }
    }

    if (it_best != states.end()) {
        // ... restore KV state via llama_state_seq_set_data_ext()
        prompt = std::move(*it_best);
        states.erase(it_best);
    }
    return true;
}
```

Key detail: a cached entry is only selected if it **strictly dominates** the current best on *both* metrics (`f_keep_best < f_keep_cur && sim_best < sim_cur`). This prevents picking a cache hit that's good on one axis but terrible on the other.

