This optimizes context-shift recovery for conversational workloads. When the context window fills and needs to shift, the server can restore a checkpoint that covers all the *previous* conversation (already cached) and only re-process the latest user message + generation. Without this, checkpoints could land mid-conversation and force re-processing of messages that are already in the prompt cache.

